[ 2026-10-09 16:08:29,095 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9e133949-fe50-4bfd-857a-3b3435de606e', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert Mechanical Engineering Assistant.\n\nProblem Categories: ['pressure_vessel', 'bolt_strength']\nTarget Operations: ['longitudinal_stress', 'tensile_stress']\nExtracted Parameters: {'D': 0.5, 'P': 2.5, 'd_bolt': 12.0, 'sigma_allow': 150.0}\nAssociated Units: {'D': 'm', 'P': 'MPa', 'd_bolt': 'mm', 'sigma_allow': 'MPa'}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the target operations and extracted parameters along with their specific units.\n2. Convert parameter units if needed before performing calculations.\n3. Invoke the necessary calculation/conversion tools using the exact numerical values and appropriate units.\n4. If multiple operations are required, execute all relevant tools in proper sequence.\n5. Do not invent or fabricate missing parameters.\n"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'A cylindrical pressure vessel with an internal diameter of $D = 0.5\\text{ m}$ ($500\\text{ mm}$) is subjected to an internal gage pressure of $P = 2.5\\text{ MPa}$ ($2,500,000\\text{ Pa}$). The cylinder end cover (flange) is secured using a ring of metric steel bolts.Given Data:Internal Vessel Diameter ($D$): $0.5\\text{ m}$Internal Pressure ($P$): $2.5\\text{ MPa}$Bolt Diameter ($d_{\\text{bolt}}$): $12\\text{ mm}$ ($0.012\\text{ m}$)Allowable Tensile Stress of Bolt Material ($\\sigma_{\\text{allow}}$): $150\\text{ MPa}$ ($150,000,000\\text{ Pa}$)Calculate:Total Pressure End Force ($F_{\\text{total}}$): The total axial force exerted by the fluid pressure on the end cover in $\\text{kN}$.Stress Area per Bolt ($A_{\\text{bolt}}$): The cross-sectional tensile area of a single $12\\text{ mm}$ bolt in $\\text{mm}^2$.Maximum Load per Bolt ($F_{\\text{bolt}}$): The maximum allowable axial load a single bolt can carry in $\\text{kN}$.Minimum Number of Bolts ($N$): The minimum number of bolts required to safely hold the end cover without exceeding the allowable tensile stress.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'beam_stress', 'description': "Calculate beam stresses and internal forces.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. bending_stress\n    Formula:\n        sigma = M * c / I\n\n    Required:\n        moment\n        c\n        inertia\n\n2. shear_stress\n    Formula:\n        tau = V * Q / (I * b)\n\n    Required:\n        force\n        first_moment_area\n        inertia\n        width\n\n3. bending_moment\n    Formula:\n        M = F * d\n\n    Required:\n        force\n        distance\n\n4. shear_force\n    Formula:\n        V = F\n\n    Required:\n        force\n\nParameters:\n    force:\n        Applied or internal force.\n\n    distance:\n        Perpendicular distance from force to the beam's\n        reference point.\n\n    moment:\n        Bending moment.\n\n    c:\n        Distance from the neutral axis to the outermost\n        fiber.\n\n    inertia:\n        Second moment of area (I).\n\n    area:\n        Cross-sectional area.\n\n    first_moment_area:\n        First moment of area (Q).\n\n    width:\n        Cross-sectional width at the location where\n        shear stress is being calculated.\n\nReturns:\n    Calculated engineering quantity as a float.", 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['bending_stress', 'shear_stress', 'bending_moment', 'shear_force'], 'type': 'string'}, 'force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'distance': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'c': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'inertia': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'first_moment_area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'width': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'bolt_strength', 'description': 'Calculate bolt tensile stress, shear stress, bolt strength,\nor recommended preload.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. TENSILE STRESS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nTensile stress:\n\n    sigma = F / A_t\n\nwhere:\n\n    F   = tensile force [N]\n    A_t = tensile stress area [m^2]\n\nIf tensile_area is not provided, the tool approximates the\narea using the nominal bolt diameter:\n\n    A = pi*d^2 / 4\n\nNote:\n    For threaded bolts, the actual tensile stress area is\n    smaller than the nominal shank area. For accurate bolt\n    calculations, provide tensile_area.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. SHEAR STRESS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nAverage shear stress:\n\n    tau = F / A_s\n\nwhere:\n\n    F   = shear force [N]\n    A_s = shear area [m^2]\n\nIf shear_area is not provided, the tool approximates:\n\n    A_s = pi*d^2 / 4\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. BOLT STRENGTH\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nCalculate the maximum tensile load based on tensile strength:\n\n    F_max = sigma_u * A_t\n\nIf yield_strength is provided, the yield load is also\ncalculated conceptually as:\n\n    F_y = sigma_y * A_t\n\nThis operation returns the tensile load corresponding to\ntensile_strength.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n4. PRELOAD\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nRecommended preload:\n\n    F_preload = k * F_proof\n\nwhere:\n\n    k = preload factor\n    F_proof = proof load\n\nIf proof_strength is provided:\n\n    F_proof = proof_strength * A_t\n\nTherefore:\n\n    F_preload = preload_factor * proof_strength * A_t\n\nIf proof_strength is not supplied, tensile_strength is used\nas a fallback.\n\nTypical preload factor:\n    0.7\n\nUnits:\n    Force -> N\n    Diameter -> m\n    Area -> m^2\n    Stress/strength -> Pa\n\nImportant:\n    This is a basic fastener-strength calculator.\n    Real bolt design may require thread geometry, bearing\n    stress, joint stiffness, fatigue, tightening torque,\n    friction, eccentric loading, and standards such as\n    ISO 898-1 or ASME specifications.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['tensile_stress', 'shear_stress', 'bolt_strength', 'preload'], 'type': 'string'}, 'force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'tensile_area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'shear_area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'tensile_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'yield_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'preload_factor': {'default': 0.7, 'type': 'number'}, 'proof_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'pressure_vessel', 'description': 'Calculate stresses and required wall thickness for a\nthin-walled cylindrical pressure vessel.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n1. HOOP STRESS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nCircumferential/hoop stress:\n\n    sigma_h = P*r/t\n\nor:\n\n    sigma_h = P*D/(2*t)\n\nwhere:\n\n    P = internal pressure\n    r = vessel internal radius\n    D = vessel internal diameter\n    t = wall thickness\n\nHoop stress is the stress around the circumference of\nthe vessel.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n2. LONGITUDINAL STRESS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nLongitudinal stress:\n\n    sigma_L = P*r/(2*t)\n\nor:\n\n    sigma_L = P*D/(4*t)\n\nFor a closed-end thin-walled cylindrical vessel:\n\n    sigma_h = 2 * sigma_L\n\n---------------------------------------------------------\n3. WALL THICKNESS\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\nRequired wall thickness based on hoop stress:\n\n    t = P*r / (S*E)\n\nor:\n\n    t = P*D / (2*S*E)\n\nwhere:\n\n    S = allowable material stress\n    E = weld/joint efficiency\n\nUnits:\n    pressure       -> Pa\n    radius/diameter -> m\n    thickness      -> m\n    stress         -> Pa\n\nExample:\n    pressure = 1 MPa\n    diameter = 1 m\n    allowable_stress = 100 MPa\n    weld_efficiency = 1.0\n\nImportant:\n    This is a thin-wall analytical calculator.\n    Real pressure-vessel design should follow the applicable\n    code/standard such as ASME Section VIII and consider\n    corrosion allowance, openings, nozzles, temperature,\n    external pressure, weld details, fatigue, and safety\n    factors.\n\n    For wall_thickness, the hoop-stress criterion is used\n    because hoop stress is the larger principal stress.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['hoop_stress', 'longitudinal_stress', 'wall_thickness'], 'type': 'string'}, 'pressure': {'type': 'number'}, 'radius': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'wall_thickness_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'allowable_stress': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'weld_efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation', 'pressure'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 